<setup>
  <selectFromSequence name="k" from="8" to="10" step="1"/>
  <selectFromSequence name="pm" from="-1" to="1" step="2"/>
  <selectFromSequence name="b" from="0" to="2" step="2"/>
  <math name="c" simplify>$pm*$k</math>
  <function name="f">$c*e^(-x/4)*sin(pi/2*x)</function>
  <function name="F">-4*$c/(1+4*pi^2)*e^(-x/4)*(sin(pi/2*x)+2*pi*cos(pi/2*x))</function>
  <math name="A1"><round numDecimals="2">abs($$F(2)-$$F(0))</round></math>
  <math name="A2"><round numDecimals="2">abs($$F(4)-$$F(2))</round></math>
  <math name="A3"><round numDecimals="2">abs($$F(6)-$$F(4))</round></math>
</setup>

<p>
  Consider the function <m>f(x)</m> whose graph is pictured below, and let <m>A_1</m> be the area the function bounds along with the <m>x</m>-axis on the interval <m>[0,2]</m>.  Similarly, let <m>A_2</m> be the area the function bounds on the interval <m>[2,4]</m> and <m>A_3</m> be the area the function bounds on the interval <m>[4,6]</m>.
</p>

<graph size="small" xmin="-1" xmax="7" ymin="-10" ymax="10" showNavigation="false" fixAxes="true"><shortDescription>graph showing a function whose y values are sometimes above and sometimes below the x-axis. </shortDescription>
  $f
  <label anchor="(3,$$f(3) - $pm)"><m>f(x)</m></label>
  <regionBetweenCurveXAxis function="$f" boundaryValues="0 2" styleNumber="3"/>
  <regionBetweenCurveXAxis function="$f" boundaryValues="2 4" styleNumber="4"/>
  <regionBetweenCurveXAxis function="$f" boundaryValues="4 6" styleNumber="5"/>
</graph>

<p>
  Suppose we know that <m>A_1 = $A1</m>, <m>A_2 = $A2</m>, and <m>A_3 = $A3</m>.  Use properties of the definite integral to determine each of the following quantities.
</p>

<p>
  <ol marker="a.">
    <li>
      <p>
        <answer><label><m>\displaystyle \int_2^4 f(x) \, dx = </m></label>-$pm*$A2</answer>
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        <answer><label><m>\displaystyle \int_$b^{<math simplify>$b+4</math>} f(x) \, dx = </m></label>
          <conditionalContent>
            <case condition="$b=0">
              $pm($A1-$A2)
            </case>
            <case condition="$b=2">
              $pm(-$A2+$A3)
            </case>
          </conditionalContent></answer>
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        <answer><label><m>\displaystyle \int_0^6 f(x) \, dx = </m></label>$pm*($A1-$A2+$A3)</answer>
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        <answer><label><m>\displaystyle \int_0^6 |f(x)| \, dx = </m></label>$A1+$A2+$A3</answer>
      </p>
    </li>
  </ol>
</p>